 "_about": "Follow-up schedules. Child immunisation follows the Ghana Health Service routine schedule (ghs.gov.gh/immunisation, checked November 2026; the page leaves the first Penta visit unlabelled, it is given here as 6 weeks). Antenatal contacts follow the WHO 8-contact model. Postnatal checks follow WHO timing (within 48 hours, day 3, day 7, week 6). The district must confirm all three before the pilot. Minimum gaps: when a dose in the Penta, OPV, PCV, Rota or malaria vaccine series is given late, the next one is scheduled at least 28 days after it (the 'after' field on a visit). Catch-up rules beyond this must come from the district.",
